# Native grid covers

The generated 3D block-letter thumbnail is the **grid cover** wherever a platform API allows a cover that is separate from the video or album body.

## Always

- Generate the thumbnail for finished video passthrough (`Thumbnail_Mode=Yes`). Do not skip covers because Remotion, VO, or crops are skipped.
- Keep `Thumbnail_URL` on Platform Outputs even when `Studio_Effective_Thumbnail_Mode` is `No`. Mode `No` skips **lettering on the video**, not the native cover.
- Stage covers onto `https://media.chicagoshining.com/publish/` or `studio/previews/` before Graph/YouTube fetch. Drive `uc?id=` / `webContentLink` is not a cover_url.

## Platform behavior

| Surface | Cover |
|---|---|
| Instagram Reel | Graph `cover_url` from the public thumbnail. Do **not** send `thumb_offset` when `cover_url` is present (offset wins and shows a video frame). |
| Facebook Reel | Graph `/{video-id}/thumbnails?is_preferred=true` with the public thumbnail URL. |
| YouTube Short | `thumbnails.set` after processing. |
| Instagram Carousel / FB multi-image | First slide **is** the grid. Prepend the 3D cover as child/slide 1 when Include Thumbnail is on. Remaining slides stay the photos. |
| Instagram Single Image | No separate cover. The image *is* the post — do not replace the photo with the 3D still. |
| Instagram/Facebook Story | Ephemeral; no profile grid cover. |
| TikTok Content Posting draft | API does not accept a cover. Keep the thumbnail in Studio/Airtable/email. Operator sets cover in the TikTok app. |

Suggested times, mix, and Remotion are unrelated. Do not treat a missing IG Reel cover as “thumbnail not needed.”
